♪ (crowd) No: reuse the tested one. ♪

211
00:12:32.453 --> 00:12:35.263
♪ Your pinned library gets a security fix? ♪

212
00:12:35.263 --> 00:12:37.073
♪ (crowd) Update on purpose, then test. ♪

213
00:12:37.073 --> 00:12:41.493
♪ Your old date code now runs for users in Europe? ♪

214
00:12:41.493 --> 00:12:43.603
♪ (crowd) Check if it assumes month first. ♪

215
00:12:43.603 --> 00:12:47.793
♪ Two apps share a module, and their needs drift apart? ♪

216
00:12:47.793 --> 00:12:49.553
♪ (crowd) Version it, or clone and own. ♪

217
00:12:49.553 --> 00:12:54.573
♪ pytest runs the tests you wrote: library or framework? ♪

218
00:12:54.573 --> 00:12:57.967
♪ (crowd) Framework: it calls your code. ♪

219
00:12:58.267 --> 00:13:03.454
(narrator) The final chorus completes the hall's belfries and roofs and the building site's upper wall courses.

220
00:13:03.454 --> 00:13:06.878
(narrator) Each question appears in turn beside the growing gold brick tower.

221
00:13:06.878 --> 00:13:14.608
(narrator) Case tags connect each question to its example: Ariane 5 for assumptions, left-pad for dependencies, urllib3 and Heartbleed for pinning and updating.

222
00:13:14.608 --> 00:13:17.617
(narrator) The final takeaway lights, and paper confetti drifts down.

223
00:13:18.220 --> 00:13:20.080
♪ Before you reuse, ask: ♪

224
00:13:20.080 --> 00:13:22.380
♪ What will it save? What will it cost? ♪

225
00:13:22.380 --> 00:13:24.220
♪ What does it assume? ♪

226
00:13:24.220 --> 00:13:26.620
♪ What does it pull in? ♪

227
00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:29.160
♪ Pin it, but update for patches. ♪

228
00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:34.900
♪ External reuse is not a one-time investment. ♪

229
00:13:36.100 --> 00:13:43.431
(narrator) The outro: your hero stays on top of the completed right-hand tower, singing and facing a central terminal that shows npm install left-pad.

230
00:13:43.431 --> 00:13:47.176
(narrator) A JavaScript example replaces the terminal: String of str dot padStart.

231
00:13:47.176 --> 00:13:48.916
(narrator) Eleven lines become one built-in.

232
00:13:48.916 --> 00:13:56.405
(narrator) Directly over the site, five case bricks stack into one build: reuse done right, and the foreman, carrying a gold brick, gives it a thumbs-up.

233
00:13:56.405 --> 00:13:59.781
(narrator) Behind it, the crane sets its prebuilt module onto the building.

234
00:13:59.781 --> 00:14:02.313
(narrator) The sun has risen to the right into golden hour.

235
00:14:02.313 --> 00:14:07.639
(narrator) The upper sky is bright blue, the horizon glows gold, and the clouds have peach and cream undersides.

236
00:14:07.639 --> 00:14:09.538
(narrator) The stars and site lamps have faded.

237
00:14:09.538 --> 00:14:17.397
(narrator) In the last seconds a blue flag with a gold brick runs up a pole on the hall’s tower, confetti falls, and the foreman salutes and gives a little hop.

238
00:14:17.980 --> 00:14:20.580
npm install left-pad?

239
00:14:20.580 --> 00:14:25.080
No need: padStart is built in.

240
00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:28.520
That's reuse done right.

241
00:14:28.520 --> 00:14:35.667
[music]
